TY  - JOUR
TI  - Selective leaching of rare earth elements from spent NiMH battery anodes using sulfuric acid
AB  - Spent nickel-metal hydride battery anodes (LaNi5-type) were leached with H2SO4. Under optimal conditions 97% of La and 93% of Nd were dissolved, followed by selective precipitation of rare earth double sulfate salts with 90% purity. Iron removal by adjusting pH to 2.5 was required before precipitation.
AU  - Wang, Fang
