TI  - Rare earth elements in agricultural soils of a mining area: distribution, source apportionment and ecological risk
AB  - Concentrations and fractionation patterns of rare earth elements (REEs) were determined in agricultural soils surrounding a Bayan Obo mining area. Source apportionment identified mining dust as the dominant contributor. Ecological risk assessment indicated moderate enrichment of La, Ce and Nd. No recovery process was investigated.
