TI  - In-situ leaching of ion-adsorption rare earth ores with magnesium sulfate: process optimization
AB  - MgSO4 leaching was investigated as an ammonium-free alternative for in-situ mining of ion-adsorption rare earth deposits. Column leaching experiments achieved 92% REO recovery with reduced ammonia-nitrogen pollution. Leachate was further concentrated and precipitated as mixed rare earth carbonate.
